      "text": "- small datasets\n- when you need a stable sort\n- nearly sorted arrays (with optimization)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- small datasets\n- when you need a stable sort\n- nearly sorted arrays (with optimization)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "S9jlorKFeVwrmo0h6AtjX",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 549.6986875715625,
      "y": 1748.5420824176476,
      "width": 791.9990234375,
      "height": 1025,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0N",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 749418449,
      "version": 1927,
      "versionNonce": 1336164691,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1772777912950,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Let's understand using array: `[90, 13, 2, 54, 6, 5, 54]`\n\nOuter Loop (i) Visualization\n- Outer loop controls how many passes we need\n- After each pass, one element gets fixed at the end\nPass 1: [90, 13, 2, 54, 6, 5, 54] → [13, 2, 54, 6, 5, 54, |90|]\nPass 2: [13, 2, 54, 6, 5, 54, |90|] → [2, 13, 6, 5, 54, |54, 90|]\nPass 3: [2, 13, 6, 5, 54, |54, 90|] → [2, 6, 5, 13, |54, 54, 90|]\nPass 4: [2, 6, 5, 13, |54, 54, 90|] → [2, 5, 6, |13, 54, 54, 90|]\nPass 5: [2, 5, 6, |13, 54, 54, 90|] → [2, 5, |6, 13, 54, 54, 90|]\nPass 6: [2, 5, |6, 13, 54, 54, 90|] → [2, |5, 6, 13, 54, 54, 90|]\n(| marks elements that are in their final position)\n\nInner Loop (j) Visualization\nDetailed view of first pass - how inner loop compares adjacent elements:\nStep 1: [90, 13, 2, 54, 6, 5, 54]\n        ↑    ↑    Compare 90,13 → Swap\n        j   j+1\n\nStep 2: [13, 90, 2, 54, 6, 5, 54]\n             ↑   ↑   Compare 90,2 → Swap\n             j   j+1\n\nStep 3: [13, 2, 90, 54, 6, 5, 54]\n                ↑    ↑  Compare 90,54 → Swap\n                j    j+1\n\nStep 4: [13, 2, 54, 90, 6, 5, 54]\n                   ↑  ↑  Compare 90,6 → Swap\n                   j  j+1\n\nStep 5: [13, 2, 54, 6, 90, 5, 54]\n                       ↑   ↑  Compare 90,5 → Swap\n                       j  j+1\n\nStep 6: [13, 2, 54, 6, 5, 90, 54]\n                          ↑   ↑  Compare 90,54 → Swap\n                         j   j+1\n\nFinal:  [13, 2, 54, 6, 5, 54, 90]\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Let's understand using array: `[90, 13, 2, 54, 6, 5, 54]`\n\nOuter Loop (i) Visualization\n- Outer loop controls how many passes we need\n- After each pass, one element gets fixed at the end\nPass 1: [90, 13, 2, 54, 6, 5, 54] → [13, 2, 54, 6, 5, 54, |90|]\nPass 2: [13, 2, 54, 6, 5, 54, |90|] → [2, 13, 6, 5, 54, |54, 90|]\nPass 3: [2, 13, 6, 5, 54, |54, 90|] → [2, 6, 5, 13, |54, 54, 90|]\nPass 4: [2, 6, 5, 13, |54, 54, 90|] → [2, 5, 6, |13, 54, 54, 90|]\nPass 5: [2, 5, 6, |13, 54, 54, 90|] → [2, 5, |6, 13, 54, 54, 90|]\nPass 6: [2, 5, |6, 13, 54, 54, 90|] → [2, |5, 6, 13, 54, 54, 90|]\n(| marks elements that are in their final position)\n\nInner Loop (j) Visualization\nDetailed view of first pass - how inner loop compares adjacent elements:\nStep 1: [90, 13, 2, 54, 6, 5, 54]\n        ↑    ↑    Compare 90,13 → Swap\n        j   j+1\n\nStep 2: [13, 90, 2, 54, 6, 5, 54]\n             ↑   ↑   Compare 90,2 → Swap\n             j   j+1\n\nStep 3: [13, 2, 90, 54, 6, 5, 54]\n                ↑    ↑  Compare 90,54 → Swap\n                j    j+1\n\nStep 4: [13, 2, 54, 90, 6, 5, 54]\n                   ↑  ↑  Compare 90,6 → Swap\n                   j  j+1\n\nStep 5: [13, 2, 54, 6, 90, 5, 54]\n                       ↑   ↑  Compare 90,5 → Swap\n                       j  j+1\n\nStep 6: [13, 2, 54, 6, 5, 90, 54]\n                          ↑   ↑  Compare 90,54 → Swap\n                         j   j+1\n\nFinal:  [13, 2, 54, 6, 5, 54, 90]\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "aUdgcn2sHf83_P6ciAF5B",
